# Project runs in graph-manager: run homes, Runs list, Start run, run page, resume, open_start_run

## What to build
A graph-manager project (store `projects`, folder `<workspacesDir>/.projects/<id>/`, a git repo holding `project.json` and `repos/<name>` links) can now be run like a workspace (spec goal **MR-08**, plus the `open_start_run` part of **MR-02**). Everywhere graph-manager resolves a workspace id for runs, the id `project~<id>` resolves to the project folder through ONE new resolver, `resolveRunHome`, in a new file `apps/graph-manager/src/server/runhome.ts`. It is used by `GET /api/runs` (list + `?workspace=` filter), `GET /api/runs/:ws/:runId`, `POST /api/runs/:ws`, `GET /api/workspaces/:id/run-defaults`, the run-page proxy `/runs/<ws>/<runId>/view/`, and resume. A project run is a multi-repo suite (`<project>/.graph-execution/suite-<rid>/suite.json`); `RunSummary` gains `project?: { id, name, repos: string[] }`. The Runs page shows a project chip with the repo names and lists projects after workspaces in its filter; the Start run drawer offers projects after workspaces, shows a check per repo (`specs/<name>.md`, `tasks/<name>/`) plus `contract.md` and `test-plan.json`, and starts `graph-execution suite --project . --provider <p> [options] --web` in the project folder with the reviewers file passed as for any run. The run page shows a project run (live: the proxied suite page; not live: a static card with the repos) and can resume it. `open_start_run` called from a project terminal (or with `project: true`) queues a request carrying `projectId`, which opens the project's Start run drawer.

NOT in this task (later tasks do them, do not build them here): sandboxed project runs (a project start or resume with `sandbox: true` answers 400 here, and the drawer disables the switch for a project); Create PR for a project run (the PR panel is not shown for project runs here); engine changes of any kind.

## What already exists (delivered by the dependencies; read the files, don't rebuild them)
- Engine (`packages/graph-execution/src/suite/`): `graph-execution suite --project <dir> --provider <p> [--model m] [--concurrency n] [--no-merge] [--human-review|--no-human-review] [--reviewers <file>] [--web]`; it also reads a non-empty `GRAPH_EXECUTION_REVIEWERS` env var as the reviewers file. `suite --resume --run <suite-id> --web` resumes from the project folder. With `--web` it detaches and prints `Started suite suite-<rid> in the background: <url>` (or `Suite suite-<rid> started: <url>`), see `packages/graph-execution/src/launch/launch.ts` (~lines 113–116). The suite id is generated by the engine (`suite-${generateRunId()}`, `suite/orchestrator.ts` ~line 157): graph-manager cannot choose it yet, so it MUST read it from stdout.
- `suite.json` (`suiteStateSchema`, exported from `graph-execution/api`) gained optional fields: `project?: { dir, name, contract }`; per feature `repo?: { name, path, startingCommit, startBranch? }`; top-level `repos?: { name, path, startingCommit, startBranch?, applied?: { files, conflicts } }[]`.
- graph-manager `src/server/projects.ts` exports `PROJECTS_DIR` (`".projects"`), `PROJECT_FILE`, `Project` (`{ id; name; workspaces: string[]; createdAt }`), `projectDirOf(workspacesDir, id)` = `<workspacesDir>/.projects/<id>`, `projectIdOf`, `repoNamesOf`, `createProjectFolder`, `syncProjectFolder`, `removeProjectFolder` (read the file for their signatures; reuse `repoNamesOf` for the repo link names if it fits). Store field `projects: Record<id, { name, workspaces, createdAt }>` (default `{}`) with methods `store.projects()` and `store.project(id)` in `src/server/store.ts`. Routes `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/projects` in `src/server/routes/projects.ts`; `GET /api/projects` answers `{ projects: [{ id, name, forge, createdAt, path, workspaces: [{ id, fullPath, repo }] }] }` (`repo` = the repo's name in project.json; names outside `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` became `-`, and they are stable across PATCH).
- `src/server/liverun.ts` exports `liveRunIn(ctx, { id, path })` (whether a run is live in a home; projects call it with id `project~<id>`). Sandbox records of a project are keyed `project~<id>/<runId>`.
- Web hooks: `src/web/useProjects.ts` (the projects of `GET /api/projects`, `[]` on error) and `src/web/useAgents.ts`.
- `project.json` in the project folder: `{ "name": "billing", "repos": [{ "name": "api", "path": "repos/api" }, …] }`; `repos/<name>` is a symlink (junction on Windows) to the workspace checkout.
- Terminals: `POST /api/terminals { projectId }` opens a terminal in the project folder; `TerminalInfo.projectId?: string` (server `src/server/terminals.ts` and web `src/web/types.ts`).

